  "question": {
    "text": "If the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;continuous at each point in its domain and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is _________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Apply L&#39;Hospital rule for an indeterminate form of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math>, we get,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>",
